// Why this file exists (2026-08-18):
//
// pi-lens auto-formats every edited JS/TS with Biome. With NO formatter config
// in the repo it does not run Biome on its defaults — it samples the file,
// guesses the indentation, and forces it onto Biome with `--indent-style space
// --indent-width 1`. This repo is tab-indented, the guess misfired, and every
// edited file got rewritten with single-space indentation: ~88k lines of churn
// across the tree on 2026-08-17 (issue #185 / PR #201). Declaring a Biome
// config here makes pi-lens defer to it instead (hasBiomeConfig short-circuits
// the guess), so the formatter always agrees with the codebase.
//
// Adoption (2026-08-18): no Biome config is a byte-identical no-op on the
// repo's pre-existing hand-written style (mixed expanded/inline collections,
// lines commonly 81-120 chars). lineWidth 80 was measured as the least-churn
// adoption point (~3.9k lines vs 7.7k at 120); the tree was reformatted once
// with `biome format --write .` and that commit landed together with this
// file. From then on, edits are stable: re-check with
// `npx @biomejs/biome format --write .` and confirm an empty diff.
//
// Load-bearing keys (a wrong value silently errors the whole config — Biome
// then formats nothing, which is easy to misread as "no-op"):
//   - trailingCommas: "all" — Biome's default is "none" and would strip the
//     repo's trailing commas. Note the 2.5.x rename: trailingCommas (plural).
//   - lineWidth: 80 — wrapped by Biome when exceeded; do not change without
//     re-running the whole-tree format and confirming the diff you expect.
//   quoteStyle "double" and semicolons "always" match Biome's defaults but are
//   pinned here as the declared convention.
//
// Run it: npx @biomejs/biome format --write .
{
	"$schema": "https://biomejs.dev/schemas/2.5.6/schema.json",
	"formatter": {
		"indentStyle": "tab",
		"indentWidth": 2,
		"lineWidth": 80
	},
	"javascript": {
		"formatter": {
			"quoteStyle": "double",
			"semicolons": "always",
			"trailingCommas": "all"
		}
	}
}
